    "Lindbladian[{a, b1, b2, ...}] or Lindbladian[a, {b1, b2, ...}] returns \
the superoperator (in the Supermap form) generating the Markovian quantum \
operation associated with the effective Hamiltonian a and the Lindblad \
operators b1, b2, .... Lindbladian[{a, None}] or Lindbladian[a, None] assumes \
that all Lindblad operators vanish. Lindbladian[{None, b1, b2, ...}] or \
Lindbladian[None, {b1, b2, ...}] assumes that the effective Hamiltonian \
vanishes, which is useful in the interaction picture. \
Lindbladian[...][\\[Rho]] transforms linear operator \\[Rho].", 
